 "_comment": "The top-level modules of Python's own library, which the bill of materials lists under Python when the app's code imports them (backlog 0402): a flaw in one is fixed in a newer Python, and matters only if the code imports it. Python's own list, sys.stdlib_module_names, without the private ones starting with an underscore, from Python 3.13.5. Made with: python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.dumps(sorted(m for m in sys.stdlib_module_names if not m.startswith('_'))))\". A module a later Python adds, or one an older Python had and dropped (distutils, imp), is missing or extra here: re-make it when a new Python is out. removed_in_later_pythons: modules Python 3.12 and 3.13 dropped (PEP 594, PEP 632, and imp), kept so an app on an older Python is still read right.",
